## Fix Graph Chat tool calls failing for users with a non-ASCII display name

Context:
On the LGE Korea workspace every Graph Chat tool call (get_status,
list_entity_types, query_graphql, triples/find, ...) failed with
`'ascii' codec can't encode characters in position 0-5: ordinal not in
range(128)` (logged at `agents.agent_dtwin_chat.tools | tools._error:139`)
for users whose Databricks display name is Korean. Databricks Apps sends
`X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` as the UTF-8 display name; Starlette decodes
header bytes as latin-1, so the router saw a str with non-ASCII code points.
The router forwarded every `x-forwarded-*` header onto the agent's loopback
httpx client, and httpx encodes str header values as ASCII, so building the
client raised before any request was sent. Users with ASCII names were not
affected. The same forwarding fed the Graph Interpreter and Cohort agents.

Changes:
1. src/agents/tools/loopback_http.py
   - New `loopback_forwarded_headers(headers)`: the single selection rule for
     inbound headers an agent forwards on loopback calls (`x-forwarded-*`,
     `x-real-*`, `x-csrf-token`, `referer`). Moved here from the dtwin router.
   - New `loopback_wire_headers(headers)`: encodes header values to the raw
     bytes that arrived on the wire (latin-1 re-encode of the Starlette str;
     UTF-8 for a str holding code points above U+00FF; bytes pass through).
   - `loopback_client` now builds the httpx client from wire bytes, so a
     non-ASCII value can never break a loopback call for any agent
     (Graph Chat, Graph Interpreter, Cohort). Identity headers are kept, and
     the receiving PermissionMiddleware decodes them to exactly the same
     values the outer request saw.
2. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   - `/dtwin/assistant/chat`, `/dtwin/assistant/chat/stream` and
     `/dtwin/metrics/interpret` use `loopback_forwarded_headers`.
   - Removed `_chat_forwarded_headers` and its constants, plus the inline
     filter in `/dtwin/metrics/interpret` (which now also forwards `x-real-*`
     and `referer`, like Graph Chat).
3. tests/units/agents/test_loopback_http.py (new)
   - Unit tests for header selection and wire encoding.
   - Graph Chat `get_status` through the real `loopback_client` (httpx
     MockTransport) succeeds for a Starlette-decoded Korean name, and the
     loopback receiver re-parses identical identity headers.
4. tests/units/api/test_dtwin_assistant_chat.py
   - Route test: `POST /dtwin/assistant/chat` with a UTF-8 Korean
     `x-forwarded-preferred-username` runs a tool call over the loopback
     client; the reply is the tool output and email / access-token / display
     name arrive byte-identical. Reproduced the production error before the
     fix.

Notes:
- MCP server (`src/mcp-server/server/http_client.py`, #208 acting headers)
  only forwards `x-forwarded-email` and `x-forwarded-access-token` as
  `x-ontobricks-acting-*`; both are ASCII by construction and the display
  name is never forwarded, so it is unchanged.
- This is a transport fix under `src/agents/**`; no prompt, tool schema or
  model behaviour changed, so no eval delta is required by the AI-feature
  gate.

